The problem space is small. An **Order** is a customer purchase with an id and priced items; a **Payment** is a charge against an external Stripe adapter. The module exposes validation, totaling, charge construction, receipt construction, and checkout separately. Checkout already coordinates them, so deepening primarily means concentrating responsibility at its Seam.

Any behavior-preserving design must reject empty Orders before Payment, sum `price × quantity`, submit one charge, return the receipt, and propagate failures. This illustrative sketch grounds those constraints:

```js
if (order.items.length === 0) throw new Error("empty order");
const cents = order.items.reduce((n, i) => n + i.price * i.quantity, 0);
const payment = await stripe.charge({ cents, reference: order.id });
return { orderId: order.id, paymentId: payment.id };
```

